6. Google OAuth Strategy
passport.use(
  new GoogleStrategy(
    {
      clientID: process.env.GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID,
      clientSecret: process.env.GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET,
      callbackURL: process.env.GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL,
    },
    (accessToken, refreshToken, profile, done) => {
      let user = users.get(profile.id);
      if (!user) {
        user = {
          id: profile.id,
          name: profile.displayName,
          email: profile.emails[0].value,
          twofaEnabled: false,
        };
        users.set(profile.id, user);
      }
      return done(null, user);
    }
  )
);


This is the core of Google login.

What it does:

Configures how Passport talks to Google:

clientID & clientSecret: identify your app to Google.

callbackURL: where Google will send users after login.

The callback function runs after Google verifies the user.

Inside that callback:

Passport gives you the user’s profile (name, email, id).

You either:

Find them in your “database”, or

Create a new record for first-time users.

Finally, call done(null, user) to signal a successful login.

