7. Login routes (OAuth flow)
Step 1: Start login
app.get(
  "/auth/google",
  passport.authenticate("google", { scope: ["profile", "email"] })
);


When someone visits /auth/google, Passport automatically:

Redirects them to Google’s login page.

Asks permission for their “profile” and “email”.

They log in, and Google redirects back to your app.

Step 2: Google callback
app.get(
  "/auth/google/callback",
  passport.authenticate("google", { failureRedirect: "/login" }),
  (req, res) => {
    if (req.user.twofaEnabled) {
      res.redirect("/2fa");
    } else {
      res.send(`
        <h1>Welcome, ${req.user.name}!</h1>
        <p>Email: ${req.user.email}</p>
        <a href="/enable-2fa">Enable 2FA</a>
      `);
    }
  }
);


Passport automatically exchanges Google’s code for an access token and fetches the user profile.

If authentication succeeds, req.user is filled with your user object.

If the user already has 2FA, redirect them to /2fa to verify it.

Otherwise, greet them and suggest enabling 2FA.

