8. Enable 2FA
app.get("/enable-2fa", (req, res) => {
  const user = req.user;
  if (!user) return res.redirect("/auth/google");


Only logged-in users can access this.

Generate a secret
  const secret = speakeasy.generateSecret({
    name: `ft_transcendence (${user.name})`,
  });
  user.tempSecret = secret.base32;


Speakeasy generates a random secret key unique to this user.

The key will be used by both your app and the Authenticator app to generate matching codes.

We store it temporarily until the user verifies it.

Create QR code
  QRCode.toDataURL(secret.otpauth_url, (err, dataURL) => {
    res.send(`
      <h2>Scan this QR Code in Google Authenticator</h2>
      <img src="${dataURL}" />
      <form action="/verify-2fa" method="POST">
        <input type="text" name="token" placeholder="Enter code"/>
        <button type="submit">Verify</button>
      </form>
    `);
  });
});


Converts the secret into a QR code that authenticator apps understand.

The user scans it → the app starts generating 6-digit codes every 30 s.

The otpauth:// URL format is a standard recognized by Google Authenticator and others.

