9. Verify 2FA setup
app.post("/verify-2fa", (req, res) => {
  const user = req.user;
  const token = req.body.token;

  const verified = speakeasy.totp.verify({
    secret: user.tempSecret,
    encoding: "base32",
    token,
  });


The user types the 6-digit code from their Authenticator app.

Speakeasy calculates what the code should be based on the secret and current time.

If they match → verified.

  if (verified) {
    user.twofaEnabled = true;
    user.secret = user.tempSecret;
    delete user.tempSecret;
    res.send("<h2>2FA enabled successfully!</h2>");
  } else {
    res.send("<h2>Invalid code, try again.</h2>");
  }
});


If verified:

Save the secret permanently (user.secret).

Mark twofaEnabled = true.

Delete the temporary secret.

If not, prompt them to try again.

