10. Verify 2FA at login

If a user already has 2FA enabled, we challenge them when they log in.

The form:
app.get("/2fa", (req, res) => {
  if (!req.user) return res.redirect("/auth/google");
  res.send(`
    <form action="/2fa" method="POST">
      <input type="text" name="token" placeholder="Enter 6-digit code"/>
      <button type="submit">Verify</button>
    </form>
  `);
});

Verification:
app.post("/2fa", (req, res) => {
  const user = req.user;
  const token = req.body.token;

  const verified = speakeasy.totp.verify({
    secret: user.secret,
    encoding: "base32",
    token,
  });

  if (verified) {
    res.send(`<h1>Welcome, ${user.name}! You are fully logged in ✅</h1>`);
  } else {
    res.send("<h2>Invalid 2FA code ❌</h2>");
  }
});


Compares the submitted code with what Speakeasy expects.

If correct → success.

If wrong → error.

